T(20, "20-1", "The Last Two Minutes", "Narrative", [
"Zainab pulled on her goalkeeper gloves and tapped them together. It was the last game of the season, and the Riverside Rovers were playing Oakfield. The score was two goals each. There were only two minutes left on the clock.",
"“Stay calm, Zainab,” called her coach, Mr Bell. “You can do this.” Zainab nodded, but her tummy felt as if it was full of butterflies.",
"Suddenly, an Oakfield player raced down the pitch with the ball at her feet. She was fast, and the Rovers’ defenders could not catch her. Zainab crouched low and stared at the ball. The girl swung her leg back and kicked as hard as she could.",
"Zainab leapt to her left. She stretched out her arms as far as they would go, and the ball smacked into her gloves. She held on tightly, even though it stung her hands. “Well saved!” shouted the crowd.",
"Zainab jumped to her feet and threw the ball out to Kofi, who was waiting near the halfway line. Kofi dribbled past one player, then another. He looked up and saw Priya running towards the goal all on her own. He passed the ball to her at just the right moment.",
"Priya did not stop to think. She kicked the ball into the corner of the net, and the goalkeeper could only watch it fly past. The Rovers had scored! A moment later, the referee blew her whistle three times. The match was over.",
"The team cheered and hugged one another. Mr Bell shook Zainab’s hand. “That save won us the game,” he said, smiling. Zainab looked down at her sore fingers and grinned. She did not mind the sting one little bit.",
], [
 dict(d="2b",k="short",m=1,q="What was the score at the start of the story?",a="Two goals each / 2-2.",g="Accept 2-2, two all or two goals each."),
 dict(d="2b",k="mc",m=1,q="What is Zainab’s job in the team?",opts=["Referee","Goalkeeper","Coach","Defender"],a="B"),
 dict(d="2a",k="find",m=1,q="Find and copy one word from paragraph 3 that tells you the Oakfield player ran quickly.",a="raced",g="Accept “raced” or “fast”."),
 dict(d="2d",k="short",m=1,q="Zainab’s tummy “felt as if it was full of butterflies”. How was she feeling?",a="Nervous / worried.",g="Accept nervous, worried, anxious or scared. Do not accept “hungry”."),
 dict(d="2c",k="order",m=1,q="Number the events from 1 to 4 to show the order they happened in.",items=["Priya scored a goal.","Zainab saved the shot.","Kofi dribbled past two players.","The Oakfield player kicked the ball hard."],a=[4,2,3,1],g=Q2),
 dict(d="2b",k="tf",m=1,q="Tick True or False for each sentence.",items=["Mr Bell was the referee.","Kofi passed the ball to Priya.","The Rovers lost the match."],a=["F","T","F"],g=TF),
 dict(d="2d",k="short",m=1,q="How do you know the ball was kicked very hard? Give one clue.",a="It smacked into her gloves / it stung her hands.",g="Accept either clue."),
 dict(d="2a",k="mc",m=1,q="In paragraph 4, what does the word “leapt” mean?",opts=["Walked slowly","Jumped","Fell over","Turned round"],a="B"),
 dict(d="2d",k="short",m=1,q="Why did Mr Bell say, “That save won us the game”?",a="Because if Zainab had not stopped the ball, Oakfield would have scored / the Rovers could not have scored their winning goal.",g="Accept any answer that shows the save stopped Oakfield going ahead and gave the Rovers the chance to win."),
 dict(d="2g",k="short",m=1,q="The writer says the ball “smacked” into Zainab’s gloves. Why is “smacked” a good word to use?",a="It sounds loud and hard, so we can hear how fast the ball was.",g="Accept any answer about the noise, force or speed of the ball."),
 dict(d="2d",k="short",m=1,q="At the end, Zainab “did not mind the sting one little bit”. Why not?",a="She was so happy that her team had won / she was proud of her save.",g="Accept any answer about being happy, proud or pleased with the win."),
])

T(20, "20-2", "Ladybirds in the Garden", "Information Report", [
"Ladybirds are small, round beetles that you can often find in gardens. There are more than forty kinds of ladybird in Britain. The best-known one is the seven-spot ladybird, which has a shiny red back with seven black spots.",
"A ladybird’s bright colours are a warning. Birds that might want to eat a ladybird learn to stay away, because it tastes horrible.",
"Ladybirds are a gardener’s friend. They eat tiny green insects called aphids, which chew the leaves and stems of garden plants. One ladybird can eat as many as fifty aphids in a single day. This helps roses, beans and other plants to grow well without any sprays.",
"A ladybird begins life as an egg. The female lays her eggs in small groups on the underside of a leaf, close to a lot of aphids. When the eggs hatch, the young ladybirds look nothing like their parents. They are long and grey, with orange marks, and they have six legs. These young ones are called larvae, and they are very hungry.",
"After a few weeks, each larva fixes itself to a leaf and turns into a pupa. Inside the pupa, its body slowly changes. About a week later, a new ladybird pushes its way out. At first, it is pale yellow with no spots at all. Its spots and its red colour appear after a few hours.",
"In autumn, ladybirds look for somewhere safe and dry to spend the winter. You might find a group of them tucked away in a crack in a wall, under a piece of bark or inside a dry plant stem. They sleep there until the weather turns warm again in spring.",
"If you want ladybirds to visit your garden, you can help them. Leave a few weeds and some long grass in a corner, and do not use sprays that kill insects.",
], [
 dict(d="2b",k="short",m=1,q="How many spots does a seven-spot ladybird have?",a="Seven.",g="Accept 7."),
 dict(d="2b",k="mc",m=1,q="What do ladybirds eat?",opts=["Leaves","Aphids","Seeds","Flowers"],a="B"),
 dict(d="2a",k="mc",m=1,q="In paragraph 3, what does the word “stems” mean?",opts=["The roots of a plant","The petals of a flower","The long parts that hold up a plant","Tiny insects"],a="C"),
 dict(d="2d",k="short",m=1,q="Why do birds usually leave ladybirds alone?",a="Ladybirds taste horrible and their bright colours warn birds.",g="Accept either: they taste horrible / the bright colours are a warning."),
 dict(d="2c",k="order",m=1,q="Number the stages from 1 to 4 to show how a ladybird grows.",items=["A pupa forms on a leaf.","A grey larva hatches from an egg.","A pale yellow ladybird comes out.","The female lays eggs under a leaf."],a=[3,2,4,1],g=Q2),
 dict(d="2b",k="tf",m=1,q="Tick True or False for each sentence.",items=["Ladybirds lay their eggs on the underside of leaves.","Newly hatched ladybirds look like their parents.","Ladybirds spend the winter in cracks or under bark."],a=["T","F","T"],g=TF),
 dict(d="2d",k="short",m=1,q="Why does the female ladybird lay her eggs close to lots of aphids?",a="So the young ladybirds have plenty of food when they hatch.",g="Accept any answer that links the aphids to food for the larvae. Do not accept “because aphids are green”."),
 dict(d="2a",k="find",m=1,q="Find and copy one word from paragraph 4 that tells you the young ladybirds want a lot of food.",a="hungry",g="Accept “hungry” only."),
 dict(d="2d",k="short",m=1,q="The text says ladybirds are “a gardener’s friend”. Why?",a="They eat the aphids that harm garden plants.",g="Accept any answer about eating aphids or protecting plants."),
 dict(d="2c",k="mc",m=1,q="Which of these is the best heading for paragraph 7?",opts=["How to spot a ladybird","How to make ladybirds welcome","Why ladybirds have spots","What ladybirds eat"],a="B"),
 dict(d="2d",k="short",m=1,q="Why might a gardener who does not want to use sprays be pleased to see a lot of ladybirds?",a="The ladybirds eat the aphids, so the plants stay healthy without sprays.",g="Accept any answer that links ladybirds eating aphids to healthy plants without sprays."),
])

T(20, "20-3", "Grandad's Shell Box", "Narrative", [
"Every summer, Kavi visited his grandad by the sea. Grandad had a wooden box that sat on the shelf in his front room, and it was full of shells. Kavi loved that box more than anything.",
"“Where did they all come from?” Kavi asked one evening, as he lifted out a spiral shell that was as pale as cream.",
"“From beaches all over the world,” said Grandad. “I found that one in Portugal. And this striped one came from a beach in Kenya. Your gran and I collected them on our travels.” Grandad ran a finger along each shell as if it were made of glass.",
"“I want to start a collection,” said Kavi. “Will you help me?” Grandad chuckled. “There’s no better place to start than right outside the door.”",
"The next morning, they took two buckets and walked down to the beach. The tide had gone out, and the sand was wet and shiny. Kavi bent over and soon found a tiny pink shell, then a flat white one, then a curly grey one. Grandad showed him how to pick out the whole shells and leave the broken ones.",
"By lunchtime, Kavi’s bucket was heavy. Back at the cottage, he washed each shell in warm water and laid them out on a towel to dry. Grandad gave him a small cardboard box with sections inside, like an egg carton.",
"That evening, Kavi wrote a label for every shell. He wrote where it was found and the date. His handwriting was rather wobbly, but he did his best. Then he put the box on the shelf, right next to Grandad’s wooden one.",
"“You know,” said Grandad quietly, “that is the best-looking shelf in the whole house.” Kavi smiled all the way to bedtime.",
], [
 dict(d="2b",k="short",m=1,q="Where did Grandad keep his box of shells?",a="On a shelf in his front room.",g="Accept on the shelf / in the front room."),
 dict(d="2b",k="mc",m=1,q="Which country did the striped shell come from?",opts=["Portugal","India","Kenya","England"],a="C"),
 dict(d="2a",k="find",m=1,q="Find and copy one word from paragraph 4 that tells you Grandad laughed quietly.",a="chuckled",g="Accept “chuckled” only (it is in paragraph 4)."),
 dict(d="2d",k="short",m=1,q="Grandad ran his finger along each shell “as if it were made of glass”. What does this tell you about how he felt about his shells?",a="He treated them with great care; they were precious to him.",g="Accept any answer about being careful, gentle or valuing the shells."),
 dict(d="2c",k="order",m=1,q="Number the events from 1 to 4 to show the order they happened in.",items=["Kavi wrote labels for his shells.","Kavi and Grandad went to the beach.","Kavi washed the shells.","Kavi asked about Grandad’s shells."],a=[4,2,3,1],g=Q2),
 dict(d="2b",k="tf",m=1,q="Tick True or False for each sentence.",items=["Kavi and Grandad took two buckets to the beach.","The tide was coming in.","Kavi put his shells in a box with sections."],a=["T","F","T"],g=TF),
 dict(d="2d",k="short",m=1,q="Why did Grandad tell Kavi to leave the broken shells on the beach?",a="Only whole shells are good for a collection / broken shells would not look good.",g="Accept any sensible reason about wanting whole, perfect shells."),
 dict(d="2a",k="mc",m=1,q="In paragraph 6, what does the word “sections” mean?",opts=["Colours","Separate parts","Holes","Lids"],a="B"),
 dict(d="2d",k="short",m=1,q="How can you tell Kavi was proud of his collection? Give one clue.",a="He put it next to Grandad’s box / he did his best with the labels / he smiled all the way to bedtime.",g="Accept any one sensible clue from the last two paragraphs."),
 dict(d="2e",k="mc",m=1,q="What do you think Kavi will do when he visits next summer?",opts=["Throw his shells away","Add more shells to his collection","Stay away from the beach","Give his shells to the shop"],a="B"),
 dict(d="2d",k="short",m=1,q="Why did Grandad say Kavi’s shelf was “the best-looking shelf in the whole house”?",a="To make Kavi feel proud / because he was pleased Kavi had started his own collection.",g="Accept any answer about praise, encouragement or being pleased with Kavi."),
])

T(20, "20-4", "How to Make Flatbreads", "Procedural", [
"Flatbreads are soft, warm and very tasty. You can eat them with soup, roll them around a filling or dip them into hummus. They are quick to make, and you do not need to wait for the dough to rise. Ask an adult to help you, because you will be using a hot pan.",
"You will need:",
"• 300 grams of plain flour, plus a little extra for rolling\n• half a teaspoon of salt\n• 150 grams of plain yoghurt\n• two tablespoons of olive oil\n• a rolling pin, a large bowl and a frying pan",
"Method",
"First, wash your hands. Tip the flour and the salt into the bowl and stir them together with a spoon. Next, add the yoghurt and the oil. Mix everything until it starts to come together in one lump.",
"Now use your hands to squeeze and knead the dough for about five minutes. It should feel soft and smooth, and it should not stick to your fingers. If it is too sticky, add a sprinkle of flour. If it is too dry, add a spoonful of yoghurt.",
"Cover the bowl with a clean tea towel and leave the dough for twenty minutes. This makes it easier to roll out.",
"After that, cut the dough into six equal pieces. Roll each piece into a ball. Dust your table with flour and roll each ball into a flat circle about as thick as a coin.",
"Ask your adult to heat the frying pan until it is hot. Cook one flatbread at a time. After about a minute, small bubbles will appear on top. Flip the bread over and cook the other side for a minute too. Stack the cooked flatbreads under a clean tea towel to keep them warm.",
"Serve your flatbreads while they are still warm. They are best eaten on the same day.",
], [
 dict(d="2b",k="short",m=1,q="Why should you ask an adult to help you?",a="You will be using a hot pan.",g="Accept: the pan is hot / to be safe."),
 dict(d="2b",k="mc",m=1,q="How much flour do you need?",opts=["150 grams","200 grams","300 grams","600 grams"],a="C"),
 dict(d="2b",k="find",m=1,q="Find and copy the two words that tell you what you must wash before you start.",a="your hands",g="Accept “hands”. The answer must be from the first paragraph of the method."),
 dict(d="2a",k="mc",m=1,q="In the method, what does the word “knead” mean?",opts=["To cut into pieces","To squeeze and push dough with your hands","To heat in a pan","To pour into a bowl"],a="B"),
 dict(d="2c",k="order",m=1,q="Number the steps from 1 to 4 to show the correct order.",items=["Cook each flatbread in a hot pan.","Leave the dough to rest for twenty minutes.","Mix the flour, salt, yoghurt and oil.","Roll each ball into a flat circle."],a=[4,2,1,3],g=Q2),
 dict(d="2d",k="short",m=1,q="What should you do if the dough is too dry?",a="Add a spoonful of yoghurt.",g="Accept: add some yoghurt. Do not accept “add flour”."),
 dict(d="2d",k="short",m=1,q="How can you tell that the first side of a flatbread is cooked and ready to turn over?",a="Small bubbles appear on top.",g="Accept bubbles."),
 dict(d="2d",k="short",m=1,q="Why do you think the cooked flatbreads are stacked under a tea towel?",a="To keep them warm.",g="Accept: keeps them warm / stops them going cold."),
 dict(d="2a",k="find",m=1,q="Find and copy one word from the method that means “the same size”.",a="equal",g="Accept “equal” only."),
 dict(d="2d",k="short",m=1,q="The text says flatbreads are “quick to make”. Which part of the method shows why they are quick?",a="You do not need to wait for the dough to rise / you only leave the dough for twenty minutes.",g="Accept either idea."),
 dict(d="2g",k="short",m=1,q="Why do you think the writer uses the words “First”, “Next” and “Now” at the start of some sentences?",a="To show the order of the steps.",g="Accept any answer about order, sequence or helping the reader follow the steps."),
])

T(20, "20-5", "The Train to the Sea", "Recount (Fictional)", [
"On Saturday morning, my dad woke me up before the sun was out. “Come on, Mia,” he whispered. “We have a train to catch.” I sat up straight. We were going to the seaside for the very first time.",
"At the station, the platform was full of people with bags and buckets. I held Dad’s hand tightly as the train rattled in. It was long and green, and it let out a loud hiss when it stopped. We climbed aboard and found two seats by the window.",
"The train began to move slowly, then faster and faster. Houses and gardens flashed past. I counted seven horses in one field, and then a tractor, and then a tiny church on a hill. Dad gave me a cheese sandwich, and I ate it while I watched the world zoom by.",
"After an hour, we went through a long tunnel. Everything went dark, and the windows turned into mirrors. I could see my own face looking back at me. I squeezed Dad’s arm, but he only laughed. “Wait for it,” he said.",
"Then we shot out into the light, and there it was. The sea stretched out flat and shining, as far as I could see. It was bluer than my school jumper. White birds circled above it, and their cries sounded like laughing.",
"“Is that really the sea?” I asked. “It’s so big!” Dad nodded and smiled.",
"A few minutes later, the train slowed down and stopped. The doors slid open, and a salty breeze rushed in. I jumped down onto the platform and pulled Dad towards the sand. It had been a long journey, but I did not feel tired at all.",
], [
 dict(d="2b",k="short",m=1,q="What time of day was it when Dad woke Mia?",a="Very early / before the sun was out.",g="Accept early morning or before sunrise."),
 dict(d="2b",k="mc",m=1,q="What did Dad give Mia to eat on the train?",opts=["A cheese sandwich","An apple","A biscuit","Some crisps"],a="A"),
 dict(d="2a",k="find",m=1,q="Find and copy one word from paragraph 2 that tells you the train made a loud sound when it stopped.",a="hiss",g="Accept \u201chiss\u201d only."),
 dict(d="2d",k="short",m=1,q="How do you know this was Mia’s first visit to the seaside?",a="The text says they were going to the seaside for the very first time / she asks “Is that really the sea?”",g="Accept either clue."),
 dict(d="2c",k="order",m=1,q="Number the events from 1 to 4 to show the order they happened in.",items=["The train went through a tunnel.","Mia saw the sea.","Mia and Dad waited on the platform.","The train stopped and the doors opened."],a=[2,3,1,4],g=Q2),
 dict(d="2b",k="tf",m=1,q="Tick True or False for each sentence.",items=["Mia counted seven horses in a field.","The tunnel was bright inside.","Mia was tired at the end of the journey."],a=["T","F","F"],g=TF),
 dict(d="2d",k="short",m=1,q="Why did Mia squeeze Dad’s arm in the tunnel?",a="It was dark and she felt a bit nervous / unsure.",g="Accept any answer linked to the dark or feeling nervous."),
 dict(d="2a",k="mc",m=1,q="In paragraph 5, what does the word “stretched” mean?",opts=["Bent","Spread out","Splashed","Shrank"],a="B"),
 dict(d="2g",k="short",m=1,q="Mia says the sea was “bluer than my school jumper”. Why does she make this comparison?",a="To show how bright and deep the blue was, using something she knows well.",g="Accept any answer about showing how blue the sea was."),
 dict(d="2d",k="short",m=1,q="What tells you Mia was excited at the end of the story?",a="She jumped down and pulled Dad towards the sand / she did not feel tired at all.",g="Accept either clue."),
 dict(d="2d",k="short",m=1,q="Why do you think Dad laughed and said “Wait for it” in the tunnel?",a="He knew the tunnel would end soon and the sea would appear.",g="Accept any answer about a surprise coming or the tunnel ending."),
])

T(20, "20-6", "Diwali, the Festival of Lights", "Information Report", [
"Diwali is a festival that is celebrated by millions of people around the world. It is often called the Festival of Lights. People who are Hindu, Sikh and Jain all celebrate Diwali, although they may do so for different reasons. The festival happens in autumn, usually in October or November.",
"Diwali lasts for five days. The main celebration takes place on the third day, on the night of the new moon. On this night the sky is very dark, so the many lights people put out shine even more brightly.",
"Lamps are a very important part of Diwali. Families light small clay lamps called diyas and place them on windowsills, doorsteps and along garden walls. Some people also hang strings of colourful lights outside their homes. Lighting the lamps is a way of welcoming happiness into the house.",
"Before the festival, people often clean their homes from top to bottom. They also make patterns called rangoli on the floor near the front door. A rangoli can be made with coloured powder, rice or flower petals. The bright shapes and colours are meant to welcome visitors.",
"Food is another big part of Diwali. Families cook special meals and make sweets to share. Popular sweets include laddoos, which are little round balls, and barfi, which is cut into small squares. People give boxes of sweets to their friends and neighbours as gifts.",
"Many people wear new clothes for Diwali. Families visit each other, send cards and give presents. In many places there are also firework displays at night, which fill the sky with colour.",
"Diwali is a time for families and friends to come together. Whether it is lighting a lamp, making a rangoli or sharing a sweet, each part of the festival is about joy and kindness.",
], [
 dict(d="2b",k="short",m=1,q="How many days does Diwali last?",a="Five days.",g="Accept 5."),
 dict(d="2b",k="mc",m=1,q="In which season does Diwali happen?",opts=["Spring","Summer","Winter","Autumn"],a="D"),
 dict(d="2a",k="find",m=1,q="Find and copy the name of the small clay lamps used at Diwali.",a="diyas",g="Accept \u201cdiyas\u201d (or \u201cdiya\u201d)."),
 dict(d="2b",k="tf",m=1,q="Tick True or False for each sentence.",items=["Rangoli patterns are made near the front door.","Laddoos are cut into small squares.","Only Hindu people celebrate Diwali."],a=["T","F","F"],g=TF),
 dict(d="2d",k="short",m=1,q="Why do the lights shine “even more brightly” on the main night?",a="Because the sky is very dark (new moon).",g="Accept any answer about the dark sky or no moon."),
 dict(d="2a",k="mc",m=1,q="In paragraph 4, what does the word “patterns” mean?",opts=["Meals","Designs made of shapes and colours","Clothes","Gifts"],a="B"),
 dict(d="2c",k="mc",m=1,q="Which of these is the best heading for paragraph 5?",opts=["Lamps and lights","Cleaning the home","Food and sweets","Fireworks"],a="C"),
 dict(d="2d",k="short",m=1,q="Why do you think people clean their homes before Diwali?",a="To get the house ready for visitors / to welcome happiness.",g="Accept any sensible reason about getting ready, visitors or a fresh start."),
 dict(d="2d",k="short",m=1,q="How can you tell that sharing is an important part of Diwali? Give one example from the text.",a="People give boxes of sweets to friends and neighbours / cook meals to share / give presents.",g="Accept any one example."),
 dict(d="2c",k="order",m=1,q="Number the parts of the text from 1 to 4 in the order they appear.",items=["Sweets and special meals","Lamps called diyas","How long the festival lasts","Rangoli patterns"],a=[4,2,1,3],g=Q2),
 dict(d="2g",k="short",m=1,q="The writer says Diwali is “about joy and kindness”. Which word tells us that the festival is happy?",a="joy",g="Accept \u201cjoy\u201d."),
])

